 ```bash
 grep '^\[seam\]' logs/train_attention_s0.log
-# [seam] S1 joint_order_match=<true|false>      (false raises: descriptor rows vs robot entity vs action order)
-# [seam] S2 obs_policy_dim=<int> term_major_ok=<true|false>
+# [seam] S1 joint_order_match=<true|false|unverified>  (only true passes; false or unverified raises: descriptor rows vs robot entity vs action order, all three must be compared)
+# [seam] S2 obs_policy_dim=<int> term_major_ok=<true|false|unverified>  (only true passes; false or unverified raises: policy term names must be exactly joint_pos, joint_vel, base_ang_vel, projected_gravity, actions, in that order, with history-carrying dims)
 # [seam] S3 compile=<value>
 # [seam] S4 default_pose_source=<env_init_state|qpos0-fallback>
 # [seam] S5 env_action_scale_match=<true|false>  (false raises: env action scale/offset per joint name vs sidecar sigma/q_def, rel tol 1e-6; `na` only with attention.descriptor: v1)
 ```
 
+**`unverified` means STOP.** If S1 or S2 prints `unverified` the run has raised on purpose: the env did not expose the action order (S1), or the policy observation term names or per-term history flattening (S2), so the check could not be made. Do not continue to the comparison runs; file the log and hand it back to P1 (the duck-typed upstream attribute names need fixing). `false` is a real mismatch and also stops the run. Evaluation checks the descriptor sha256 only for the attention arm.
+
 **S4 default pose source == env init state.** The descriptor default-angle column must come from the upstream robot entity config's initial joint positions (`upstream.robot_cfg_loader` in the config), not from the model `qpos0`. Expect `S4 default_pose_source=env_init_state`. `qpos0-fallback` means the loader key was removed and the descriptor does not match the env start pose. If the configured loader cannot be imported, the run fails loudly (the identifier in the config is unverified). **S5 env action scale match.** The production descriptor is v2 (`attention.descriptor: v2`, 16-d; `v1` is 12-d). Its actuator parameters (effort limit, stiffness, damping) come from the robot entity config (`upstream.robot_cfg_loader`) and the action scale sigma from `upstream.action_scale_loader`; both identifiers are unverified and the run fails loudly if they cannot be imported or do not cover all 29 joints. Expect `S5 env_action_scale_match=true`: the env action manager's per-joint scale and offset equal the sidecar `sigma` and `q_def` (`junior_policy.json` key `descriptor`, which also records the descriptor matrix sha256; eval re-checks it). The reference-table actuator values are a CPU fixture only. The trainer prints `params: world model …, policy …`. Policy params differ between arms only by the decoder: attention decoder about 0.46 M vs mlp_matched about 0.47 M.
 
